5^3 \\)\n- \\( 216 = 6^3 \\)\n- \\( 343 = 7^3 \\)\n- \\( 512 = 8^3 = (2^3)^3 = 2^9 \\)\n- \\( 729 = 9^3 = (3^2)^3 = 3^6 \\)\n\nFrom the above, we see that 512 and 729 are cubes of cubes (i.e., \\( 2^9 \\) and \\( 3^6 \\)).\n\n### Step 3: Sum the Valid Three-Digit Cubes\nThe valid three-digit cubes that are cubes of squares or cubes are 512 and 729. We sum these numbers:\n\\[ 512 + 729 = 1241 \\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{1241}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1241}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
